---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BookingLink from '../components/BookingLink.astro';
import Pricing from '../components/Pricing.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import Closing from '../components/Closing.astro';
import { faqGroups } from '../data/faq';
import { equineWarning } from '../data/legal';
import { path } from '../data/site';
import { brand } from '../data/site';
import EditorialImage from '../components/EditorialImage.astro';
---
<Layout active="horse-rider" title="Horse + Rider Performance in Colorado" description="Pilates-informed rider movement and equine bodywork with Stephanie Kopacek. Explore balance, coordination, and the horse–rider partnership in Larkspur, Colorado.">
  <section class="signature-hero"><div class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">The signature {brand.name} session</p><h1>Two athletes.<br /><em>One conversation.</em></h1><div class="signature-hero-bottom"><p>When horse and rider move together, awareness belongs on both sides of the saddle.</p><BookingLink light label="Explore your partnership" /></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Horse + rider performance</p><h2>See both sides.<br /><em>Find common ground.</em></h2></div><div class="partnership-grid"><article><span class="eyebrow">01 / Rider</span><h3>Your body.<br />Your awareness.</h3><p>Explore balance, mobility, seat, posture, strength, and control. Notice your own habits and the choices available to you.</p><span class="partnership-words">Strength · Mobility · Awareness</span></article><span class="partnership-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span><article><span class="eyebrow">02 / Horse</span><h3>Their movement.<br />Their responses.</h3><p>Observe movement, balance, and body awareness. Give the horse’s athletic function the same thoughtful attention.</p><span class="partnership-words">Movement · Balance · Performance</span></article></div><div class="together"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Together</p><h3>Communication. Coordination. Connection.</h3><p>Consider how your movement patterns meet. Explore timing, symmetry, and the sense of moving as an athletic pair.</p></div></section>
  <div class="wide-figure wrap"><EditorialImage slot="rider-in-saddle" class="wide-image" sizes="90vw" /></div>
  <section class="sage-section"><div class="wrap section editorial-split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Across the partnership</p><h2>One perspective.<br /><em>Both bodies.</em></h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Stephanie’s private Pilates instruction and equine bodywork experience allow her to consider rider and horse together. Pilates-informed movement gives the rider a way to explore their own balance, strength, mobility, and control.</p><p>Equine observation and bodywork bring attention to the horse’s side of the relationship. The session creates space to consider how the pair moves together, without promising a particular outcome.</p><p>Whether you ride recreationally or compete, the starting point is your individual partnership.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section price-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">A session built around your pair</p><h2>Make the<br /><em>connection.</em></h2><EditorialImage slot="horse-rider-connection" class="split-image" sizes="(max-width: 1023px) 90vw, 35vw" /><p class="support-copy">The session format, location, equipment, and horse participation are agreed with Stephanie in advance. Confirm arrangements before bringing your horse.</p></div><div><Pricing items={['partnership']} /><BookingLink /><p class="fine-print">Movement instruction and equine bodywork support athletic awareness and performance. They do not replace medical or veterinary care. Riding and handling horses carry inherent risks; helmets are required for any mounted work.</p><p class="fine-print statutory-warning">{equineWarning}</p><p class="fine-print">Sessions are subject to our <a class="inline-link" href={path('terms')}>terms</a>, including a signed participation agreement before your first session.</p></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section faq-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">The details</p><h2>About your session.</h2></div><Faq items={faqGroups[2].items} /></section>
  <Closing title="Move forward, together." text="A thoughtful starting point for your horse-and-rider partnership." />
</Layout>
